<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Debug builds only.

    Cleartext is permitted at the platform level here so that a head running
    on a developer's laptop can be reached without a domain and a
    certificate. The platform cannot express "private ranges only" — it
    matches domains, not subnets — so trying to scope it here produces a
    narrow list that disagrees with what the app itself accepts, and the
    symptom is an address the app takes and the system then silently drops.

    The actual gate is in the app: ApiEndpoints.normalise refuses plain HTTP
    to anything outside 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16 and localhost, and that
    rule is unit-tested. This file exists to stop the platform overriding a
    decision that has already been made properly one layer up.

    The release config permits no cleartext at all.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
